meta {
  name: Liveness
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/health/live
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 whenever the process is up and the pipeline is responsive, with an empty checks array -
  it runs no dependency checks at all, and that is the design rather than an oversight.

  A liveness probe that reached PostgreSQL would mean a database outage causes Kubernetes to
  restart every replica in a loop, which cannot help and actively hinders recovery by
  hammering the database with reconnections as each pod starts.
}
